      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Ethanol molecular ion (n-ionised at O, +. on OH) losing water by 1,2-elimination: the beta H on the methyl carbon (H4) and the OH combine as H2O while C1=C2 (ethylene) forms. Charge RETENTION: water leaves as the radical cation HOH+.. Book draws 4 fishhook barbs -- a two-barbed homolysis mark on the cleaved C1-H(beta) bond <1,4> and on the cleaved C2-O bond <2,3>; all four encoded moves are drawn (each cleaved bond sends one electron to the forming C=C pi and one to the forming O-H bond of water). The O keeps its charge+radical."
