      "curator_note": "Cross-links to IMS_4_4_row3. VERIFY: the DFS ...[C]1(H2,H3,H4)[C]5(H6,H7)[O+.]8(H9) >> [C]1(H2,H3){=}[C]5(H6,H4).[H]7[O+.]8[H]9 takes the water H from C5 (the SAME carbon that bears the OH = a 1,1-elimination) and migrates H4 from C1 onto C5. The BOOK draws a 1,2-elimination (the eliminated H sits on the OTHER carbon, the methyl). Net products identical (H2O+. + ethylene) but different H bookkeeping / mechanism: partial MISMATCH, see rule_mismatches."
